WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.160
As routers are added to networks, configurations
are changed.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.670
As routing tables are updated automatically
and manually, routers need to receive the

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.790
most recent updates to the overall network
topology.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.910
A process called convergence does this.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:19.430
In this process, a root bridge router learns
the topology of the entire network and then

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.220
distributes that topology to the remaining
routers on the network.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.660
The process can take several seconds, so if
one notices a temporary slowdown in network

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.870
performance, specifically after either physical
or logical topology changes have taken place,

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.260
convergence is probably taking place at that
time within the network.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.620
Normal traffic flow should resume once convergence
has been completed.

